<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Spoon Browser — Network Security Config

    Policy as of batch D (2026-09-30):
    The platform-level cleartext block is DISABLED here. All cleartext
    enforcement now lives in app code (CleartextPolicy + SpoonWebViewClient).

    Why the change:
    Network Security Config is compile-time only. It cannot be updated at
    runtime, so a user-editable router whitelist is impossible under it.
    For a browser, users legitimately need to reach arbitrary http:// hosts
    (routers, dev servers, LAN-only services), so the policy must be
    adjustable without a rebuild.

    Current behavior:
    - Compiled default whitelist (router brands, gateway IPs, localhost,
      emulator host, mDNS) is in CleartextPolicy.java.
    - User-added hosts are stored in the spoon_cleartext preferences.
    - SpoonWebViewClient.handleUrlLoading consults both and either allows
      the http:// load or upgrades the URL to https://.

    Tradeoff accepted:
    A bug in SpoonWebViewClient.handleUrlLoading becomes a cleartext leak.
    Previously the platform was a hard floor. Reverting this file to
    base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" restores the platform
    guarantee but also freezes the whitelist at build time.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
